        <h3>Step 1: Confirm Eligibility — Residency Period Met</h3>
        <p>Before investing time and money in exams and documents, verify that you meet one of the legal pathways to Spanish citizenship. The most common route is <strong>10 years of continuous residency in Spain</strong>. However, shorter paths exist:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>10 years general residency:</strong> Standard pathway for long-term residents.</li>
          <li><strong>5 years:</strong> For refugees, stateless persons, or other special circumstances.</li>
          <li><strong>2 years:</strong> If you are a national of an Ibero-American country, Andorra, Portugal, or Equatorial Guinea.</li>
          <li><strong>1 year:</strong> If married to a Spanish citizen or if you are a Spanish descendant or adoptee.</li>
          <li><strong>Immediate:</strong> If you are a descendant of a Spanish citizen born before 1970.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Check <a href="/spanish-citizenship-requirements.html">our eligibility guide</a> to confirm your specific pathway. If you're unsure, schedule a consultation with one of our legal advisors.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 2: Pass DELE A2 Language Test -->
      <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <h3>Step 2: Pass DELE A2 Language Test</h3>
        <p>The DELE A2 (Diplomas de Español como Lengua Extranjera) is an official Spanish proficiency exam administered by the Cervantes Institute and recognized globally. A2 is the second level in the Common European Framework of Reference (CEFR), representing basic competence in Spanish.</p>
        <p><strong>What the A2 test covers:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Reading comprehension (short texts, emails, simple documents)</li>
          <li>Writing skills (basic messages, short paragraphs)</li>
          <li>Listening comprehension (conversations, announcements)</li>
          <li>Speaking ability (simple dialogue, describing personal experiences)</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>How to prepare:</strong> The exam typically costs €120–€150 and is offered multiple times per year at certified test centers across Spain and internationally. Most preparation courses run 3–6 months. Official practice materials are available from the Cervantes Institute website. Many applicants begin preparation 4–6 months before their intended application date.</p>
        <p><strong>Timeline:</strong> You can take DELE A2 anytime once you decide to pursue citizenship, but we recommend passing it at least 3 months before submitting your application to allow time for the next steps.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 3: Pass CCSE Culture Test -->
